  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Truvalu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At Truvalu.trade, we believe in equal distribution in the value chain for all actors and stakeholders. We believe that SMEs are the drivers of (local) economies everywhere, be it in hilly landscapes of Colombia or flat industrial lines of Germany. Our focus is however dedicated to SMEs in the food and creative sectors in developing and transition countries. We support thoroughly selected SMEs through offering tailored finance and by buying their products for sales on the Dutch market. By doing so we support (rural) job creation, poverty alleviation and food security in those countries. We believe that is the fair thing to do &#x2013; business as usual! In addition, the Dutch public gets to enjoy delicious treats from across the globe! It is the objective of this project to strengthen our core activity of purchasing local natural and sustainable products that can be sold through our distribution network of WAAR stores network in The Netherlands. More specific the project will enable the purchase, shipment and distribution of 78,000+ products &#x2013; ranging from home decoration, to soaps, to chocolates &#x2013; from 12 local SMEs in Bangladesh, Indonesia, India, Sri Lanka, Kenya, Colombia and Vietnam. These SMEs provide direct jobs &#x2013; in fair and sustainable working conditions &#x2013; for about 1,400 people.</narrative>
  </description>
